    <section class="msc-learn-key-terms" aria-labelledby="MscGuide077Terms"><h2 id="MscGuide077Terms">Key Terms</h2><dl><div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Bitcoin conference</dt><dd>An organized gathering whose program focuses partly or entirely on Bitcoin.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Organizer</dt><dd>The person or entity responsible for the venue, program, funding, operations, and event rules.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Program</dt><dd>The scheduled collection of talks, workshops, panels, exhibitions, meetings, and activities.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Call for proposals</dt><dd>A process through which people submit talks, workshops, or other sessions for consideration.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Workshop</dt><dd>A session designed around guided, practical participation rather than presentation alone.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Hackathon</dt><dd>A time-limited collaborative event in which participants develop or demonstrate projects.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Technical conference</dt><dd>An event centered on engineering, protocol, security, research, or implementation work.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Regional conference</dt><dd>An event designed around a geographic community and its local context.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Sponsor</dt><dd>An organization or person that provides money, services, or resources in exchange for defined event benefits.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Sponsored session</dt><dd>Programming funded or controlled partly by a sponsor and identified as such.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Exhibition hall</dt><dd>A space where companies, projects, vendors, and organizations display or demonstrate their work.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Side event</dt><dd>A gathering scheduled around a main conference but organized separately or by a partner.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Media credential</dt><dd>Event access granted to journalists or media workers under defined terms.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Embargo</dt><dd>An agreement not to publish specified information before a stated time.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Travel grant</dt><dd>Financial support intended to reduce the cost of attending or contributing to an event.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Code of conduct</dt><dd>Rules describing expected behavior and the process for reporting violations.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Conference archive</dt><dd>Recordings, schedules, slides, photographs, or other materials preserved after an event.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Follow-up artifact</dt><dd>Code, documentation, research, recordings, funding, or project work that continues after the event.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Narrative</dt><dd>A framing or interpretation that influences how people understand an event or subject.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Access tier</dt><dd>A ticket or credential category that grants different spaces, sessions, or benefits.</dd></div></dl></section>
